The function then uses `await` to wait for the mutex to become available before proceeding with the addition process. If another instance of the application is already adding a site, this will cause the current instance to wait until the other instance has finished.

Once the mutex is acquired, the function initializes the web application within the specified directory by creating a new directory for the site and adding a new `web.config` file to it. If an exception occurs during this process, the function logs the error using the `Logger` class and returns an empty string to indicate failure.

Finally, the function releases the mutex and returns the path of the newly added web application.']

