The function will read the file, sort its lines lexicographically, and extract a sequence number from the last line, using this number to rename the file accordingly. Edge cases, such as invalid passwords, issues with file operations, or insufficient memory allocation, will be managed to avoid leaking sensitive information. Upon successful initialization, renaming, and encryption, the function will return a pointer to the cipher context, the modified filename, and a pointer to the octree structure.

The function also provides a cleanup function `cleanup` that safely disables the cipher and deallocates the octree when it is no longer needed.']

