The `IsFull` property returns `true` if the queue is full, based on the specified capacity. The `IsEmpty` property returns `true` if the queue is empty. The `Count` property returns the current number of elements in the queue.

This implementation also includes a mechanism to handle potential race conditions and ensure data integrity under concurrent access. When an item is added or removed from the queue, it is done in a thread-safe manner by locking the access to the list using the `lock` object. This ensures that only one thread can modify the list at a time, preventing race conditions and data corruption.

The `Delete` method also sets a flag indicating that the queue has been deleted, which prevents any further modifications to the queue. This is important because if the queue is not properly cleaned up after use, it can cause memory leaks or other issues.

