To handle large data volumes and high concurrency, this implementation uses a `lock` object to ensure that only one thread can modify the list at a time. This prevents race conditions and ensures data integrity under concurrent access. Additionally, the `Delete` method sets a flag indicating that the queue has been deleted, which helps to prevent memory leaks or other issues if the queue is not properly cleaned up after use.

