The function also includes functions for retrieving an element's HTML content by its ID, listing all active elements, and finding an element in the list of active elements by its ID. These functions are designed to be thread-safe and efficient, using a memory pool allocator to minimize fragmentation and ensure proper deallocation when the function is destroyed.

