The `DataGenerator` class has several properties that can be used to configure the behavior of the random number generator:

* `Seed`: The seed value used by the random number generator. Defaults to 0 if not specified.
* `Precision`: The precision of the generated numbers. Defaults to 1 if not specified.
* `Length`: The length of the generated strings. Defaults to 10 if not specified.
* `IsInclusive`: Whether to generate random numbers inclusively or exclusively within the given range. Defaults to true if not specified.
* `IsExclusive`: Whether to generate random numbers exclusively within the given range. Defaults to false if not specified.
* `MinValue`: The minimum value of the generated numbers. Defaults to double.MinValue if not specified.
* `MaxValue`: The maximum value of the generated numbers. Defaults to double.MaxValue if not specified.
* `StringValues`: An array of string values that can be used to generate random strings. If this property is set, the `GenerateString` method will return a randomly selected string from the provided array.

The `DataGenerator` class also provides several methods for generating random data:

* `GenerateInt`: Generates an integer between the specified minimum and maximum values (inclusive or exclusive).
* `GenerateFloat`: Generates a float between the specified minimum and maximum values (inclusive or exclusive).
* `GenerateDouble`: Generates a double between the specified minimum and maximum values (inclusive or exclusive).
* `GenerateString`: Generates a string with the specified length. If the `StringValues` property is set, it will return a randomly selected string from the provided array.
* `Reset`: Resets the random data generator to its initial state.

The `ToString` method overrides the default behavior of the `Object.ToString()` method and returns a string representation of the current state of the generator, including the seed value, precision, length, inclusive/exclusive range, minimum and maximum values, and any provided string values.

This code also includes performance optimizations for large-scale data generation tasks by using a `Random` object with a custom seed to ensure reproducibility. The class is also thread-safe for concurrent usage.']

