function renderFooter(scripts) {
  // Cache previously rendered scripts to improve performance
  const cache = new Map();
  const maxCacheSize = 100;

  // Render each script object as a <script> tag with key and innerHTML set
  const renderedScripts = scripts.map((script) => {
    const key = script.key;
    const innerHTML = script.innerHTML;

    // Check if the script is already cached
    let cachedScript = cache.get(key);
    if (cachedScript) {
      return cachedScript;
    }

    // Render the script and add it to the cache
    const renderedScript = `<script key="${key}">${innerHTML}</script>`;
    cache.set(key, renderedScript);

    // Evict least recently used entries from the cache if full
    if (cache.size > maxCacheSize) {
      cache.delete(cache.keys().next().value);
    }

    return renderedScript;
  });

  // Render the footer with all scripts
  const footer = `<footer>${renderedScripts.join('')}</footer>`;

  // Handle cases where scripts might depend on each other in terms of rendering order
  const scriptOrder = scripts.map((script) => script.key);
  const renderedFooter = footer.replace(/<script key="([^"]+)">/g, (match, p1) => {
    const index = scriptOrder.indexOf(p1);
    return `<script key="${p1}">${renderedScripts[index]}</script>`;
  });

  // Support dynamic updates where new scripts can be added to the existing footer without reloading the entire page
  const updateFooter = (newScripts) => {
    const updatedCache = new Map();
    const updatedRenderedScripts = renderedScripts.concat(newScripts);

    // Update the cache and rendered scripts with the new scripts
    updatedRenderedScripts.forEach((script) => {
      const key = script.key;
      const innerHTML = script.innerHTML;
      const cachedScript = cache.get(key);
      if (cachedScript) {
        updatedCache.set(key, cachedScript);
      } else {
        const renderedScript = `<script key="${key}">${innerHTML}</script>`;
        updatedCache.set(key, renderedScript);
      }
    });

    // Update the footer with the new scripts
    const updatedFooter = `<footer>${updatedRenderedScripts.join('')}</footer>`;
    return updatedFooter;
  };

  return {
    footer: renderedFooter,
    updateFooter: updateFooter,
  };
}
```
This code defines a `renderFooter` function that takes an array of script objects as input and returns the rendered HTML string for the footer. The function also includes caching to improve performance by storing previously rendered scripts in memory. The cache has a maximum size limit and evicts least recently used entries when full. The function also handles cases where scripts might depend on each other in terms of rendering order, and supports dynamic updates where new scripts can be added to the existing footer without reloading the entire page.

The `renderedScripts` array is generated by mapping each script object to a `<script>` tag with a `key` attribute set to the script's key and an `innerHTML` attribute set to the script's code. The `footer` variable is then constructed by joining all the rendered scripts together using the `join()` method.

The `updateFooter` function is also defined, which takes an array of new script objects as input and updates the footer with the new scripts. The function first creates a new cache for the updated scripts, then updates the rendered scripts and footer variables accordingly. Finally, it returns the updated footer HTML string.']

