This implementation includes a custom error handling mechanism for out-of-memory conditions, which logs errors without crashing the program. It also includes functions to reset the entire weather station system to its initial state, partially reset only the precipitation level and storm alert status, and enqueue new status messages into the ring buffer. The performance implications of reallocating memory versus updating pointers are considered when dealing with large datasets.

