The function `weather_station_reset` frees all allocated memory for the temperature readings array, linked list of sensor metadata, and ring buffer of status messages. It then reinitializes the arrays with zeros and sets the 'storm alert status' to false.

The function `weather_station_partial_reset` partially resets only the precipitation level and storm alert status in the linked list of sensor metadata.

The function `weather_station_enqueue_status` checks if the ring buffer is full, and if it is, removes the oldest message from the front of the queue by freeing its memory and moving all subsequent messages to the left. It then allocates memory for a new status message and copies the contents of the new message into the ring buffer.

The function `weather_station_init` demonstrates how to handle out-of-memory conditions gracefully, manage memory efficiently, and initialize complex data structures with default values. The functions `weather_station_reset`, `weather_station_partial_reset`, and `weather_station_enqueue_status` demonstrate how to reset the entire system to its initial state, partially reset only certain components, and enqueue new status messages into the ring buffer while maintaining efficient memory usage.']

