The function also includes a reset function that frees all allocated memory, reinitializes the arrays with zeros for all elements, sets the overload status to false, clears the error code, and truncates the event timestamps. A partial reset function is also implemented that resets only the average utilization percentage and overload status to their initial states, leaving other data unchanged.

The function also includes an update hash table function that updates the hash table with new IP addresses and descriptions, ensuring the hash table does not exceed a maximum size defined by a parameter `max_table_size`. The function handles out-of-memory conditions gracefully by logging error without crashing the program.

The code is written in C and includes comments to explain each section of the code. The functions are implemented using dynamic memory allocation, which allows for efficient memory management and avoids memory leaks. The code also includes a custom error handling mechanism that logs errors without crashing the program, ensuring that the system can continue running even under edge cases.']

