The cleanup operation releases all allocated resources efficiently, preventing memory leaks. The function supports a configurable aging policy, removing transactions older than a specified threshold to enhance efficiency. The performance impact of filtering transactions based on criteria such as length, frequency, and recent activity is evaluated, balancing accuracy with efficiency. The function also supports a configurable cache eviction policy (LRU, FIFO, etc.) and provides mechanisms for monitoring and reporting cache hit ratios, cache miss ratios, and memory usage statistics to help users fine-tune their configuration.

The implementation is thread-safe, allowing concurrent access from multiple threads while managing synchronization to prevent race conditions and maintain data integrity. The function also supports a configurable verbosity level for the logging system, enabling users to adjust the amount of information recorded in the log file.']

